# Naming and Single-Responsibility Audit: Independent Pass, Summary and Contract
File: openOODA/audits/naming/mcode.oot

Provenance: converted from `openOODA/audits/naming-audit-mcode.md` (788 lines). Part 1 of 7.

Redaction note: fleet host names and tailnet addresses are written as generic
placeholders. The audited tree still holds the literals.

# Naming & Single-Responsibility Audit — Independent Pass (mcode / MiniMax M3.1-Flash)

**Auditor:** MiniMax Code (`mcode`, MiniMax-M3.1-Flash) — Stage 1 Code Reviewer, openOODA reviewer (`w3:p1`)
**Date:** 2026-11-05
**Scope:** all 9 openOODA organizations — `/Projects/openOODA`, `/Projects/openOODA-core`, `/Projects/openOODA-kernel`,
`/Projects/openOODA-OS`, `/Projects/openOODA-tools`, `/Projects/openOODA-DE`, `/Projects/openOODA-apps`,
`/Projects/openOODA-cloud`, `/Projects/openOODA-agents`
**Method:** read-only inspection. Directory names, `README.md`, `Makefile` `BIN`/`PERSONAS`/`SRC`/`VER`, `anchor.oo`, `ooda.pkg`
, `VERSION`, persona dispatch tables, and `.oo` source headers were read directly.
**Build constraint honoured:** no compiler was invoked. No `make`, no `oodac`, no `cc`/`clang`/`gcc`/`rustc`, no build or test
target, no binary executed, no git state mutated. Only file reads, path/name search, and read-only shell (`wc`, `diff`, `awk`,
`sed`, `find -type l`, `stat`).

> **Snapshot caveat.** The `openOODA-apps` tree changed *during* this audit. `openOODA-apps/ooflash/` was created and populated
> between 03:55 and 03:58 HST on 2026-11-05, and the flasher half was deleted from `openOODA-apps/oomedia/` at ~03:59. Both the
> pre-split and post-split states were captured and are reported separately where they differ. All other claims describe the
> tree as found.

---

## 0. Executive summary

The project does **not** have a naming problem so much as a **name-ownership** problem. The vocabulary is mostly disciplined (
`oo` prefix, one repo per binary, `PERSONAS` tables, RFC 0012 consolidation targets). What is broken is the **binding between a
name and exactly one owner**.

Table columns: # | Finding | Severity
- **F1** | **82 distinct name tokens are simultaneously a standalone repo/binary and a persona of another binary.** 57 are
  served by **two or more different hosts**; 49 are repo-vs-persona collisions inside one org; 5 cross an org boundary. |
  **Critical**
- **F2** | **20 of those 82 are published in the signed public package catalog** (`catalog/index`), so the ambiguity is
  user-visible on the install surface, not just internal. | **Critical**
- **F3** | **Two mutually-recursive persona claims exist**: `oohash` claims `oob3sum` and `oob3sum` claims `oohash` (
  `oohash/ipc/dispatch_persona.oo:33`, `oob3sum/ipc/persona_dispatch.oo:32`). Neither can be archived until the cycle is broken.
  | **Critical**
- **F4** | **Two incompatible multi-call dispatch contracts are simultaneously in force.** RFC 0012 §2.2 mandates
  explicit-subcommand dispatch and Rule 1.25 bans symlinks, but `openOODA-OS/ooimage` selects personas from `sys_argv0` basename
  (`ooimage/main.oo:62`), and `website/llms.txt:35` still advertises "`sys_argv0` symlink dispatch". | **High**
- **F5** | **`openOODA-core/std` carries 112 `.oo` files of Layer-1 kernel/driver code**, duplicating `openOODA-kernel`
  responsibilities including two verbatim-identical capability-space pages. A "standard library" repo is doing kernel work. |
  **High**
- **F6** | **`openOODA-OS/ooimage` claims three responsibilities and implements one.** Its README promises Level-1 ISO and
  Level-2 UEFI/Firecracker image building; zero source implements either. The name `ooimage` is a pure overclaim. | **High**
- **F7** | **All 17 `openOODA-kernel` repos are one template**, not 17 responsibilities: the same 15 cross-cutting pages in
  every repo, differing only by a repo-name token. | **High**
- **F8** | **Absorption is declared but never enacted.** Across the fleet, absorbed repos still build and publish their own
  standalone binary, so the "one canonical binary per domain" rule is not enforced anywhere in the tree. | **High**
- **F9** | **`openOODA-apps/oomedia` was the canonical scope-pollution example** (media player + USB flasher). It has since been
  split into `ooflash` — the split is *correct in direction* but `ooflash` introduces a C-binary fallback (`dd`, `truncate`,
  `sha256sum`, `sync`) that contradicts Rule 1.25 and `roadmap.oot:90`. | **High**
- **F10** | **The consolidation spec itself has gaps.** RFC 0012 §2.3 names canonical targets that do not exist as repos, and
  leaves 30+ existing repos with no planned home. | **Medium**
- **F11** | **Documentation drift is systemic**: stale page counts, assertion counts, versions, and — in 9 repos — README lines
  advertising `ooagent-*` symlink applets that were deliberately deleted. | **Medium**
- **F12** | **Hardcoded hostnames/Tailscale IPs survive inside `.oo` sources** in `openOODA/openOODA/buildbox/` and as live
  function identifiers in `openOODA-OS/oollama`. | **Medium**

**Positive findings (also first-principles):** the **Zero Symlinks and Hardlinks Law is fully complied with** — 0 symlinks and 0
hardlinks across all 9 org trees. The **Page Rule is honoured** — exactly 1 `.oo` file exceeds 256 lines fleet-wide and it is a
deliberate negative-test fixture (`openOODA-core/oodac/tests/fixtures/boundary_257_lines.oo`). The **catalog index has zero
drift** against the 256 on-disk packages. The `oo` namespace prefix is applied consistently with a small, explicable exception
set.

---

## 1. The governing contract (what the audit measures against)

The audit is scored against the project's own written standards, not an external opinion.

Table columns: Contract | Location | Substance
- **Rule 1.25 — Zero Symlinks and Hardlinks Law** | `openOODA/openOODA/rules.oot:244-248` | Zero symlinks/hardlinks anywhere.
  Every `bin/`/`dist/` executable is a real standalone ELF (`! -L`, link count 1). Consolidated tools expose personas via
  **explicit CLI subcommands or flags**, never symlink aliases. Code sharing via `import "oostd/..."`, never filesystem links.
- **Executive Zero-Symlinks Directive** | `openOODA/zero_symlinks_directive.oot:10-16` | Codifies Rule 1.25 and names the
  canonical consolidated tools: `oohash`, `oobase64`/`oocodec`, `ooarchive`, `oosort`/`ootext`, `ooherdr`, `oocode`, `oocomp`,
  `oopanel`, `oostore`, `oooda-engine`, `ooconsensus`.
- **RFC 0012 — Unix Less-Is-More Consolidation** | `openOODA/openOODA/rfcs/0012-unix-less-is-more-consolidation.oot` | §2.2
  defines persona tables and the zero-link rule. §2.3 sets the consolidation target: **377 → 129 canonical repos**, with a
  per-org target list.
- **Roadmap** | `openOODA/openOODA/roadmap.oot:81,90` | `ooflash` listed as a backlog item ("separated from `oomedia` media
  player"). `2026-11: Deprecate non-sandboxed subprocess execution shims across all tooling.`
